---
import ArticleLayout from '../../layouts/ArticleLayout.astro';
import { siteContact } from '../../data/site';
---
<ArticleLayout title="Privacy policy" description="How the independently operated Child Savings Lab handles browser-only calculator inputs, Cloudflare hosting information, email correspondence, and privacy requests." effective="Effective October 8, 2026">
  <h2>Operator and contact</h2>
  <p>Child Savings Lab is an individually operated educational publication. The independent publisher is responsible for this website’s privacy practices. Contact the publisher at <a href={siteContact.emailHref}>{siteContact.email}</a> with questions or privacy requests.</p>
  <h2>Audience</h2>
  <p>Child Savings Lab is an adult-directed educational service for parents, guardians, employers, and other adults researching family-finance topics. It is not designed for children under 13, does not offer child accounts, and does not knowingly request personal information directly from children.</p>
  <h2>Calculator data</h2>
  <p>Eligibility and growth calculator inputs, including the birth date and contribution assumptions you enter, are processed by JavaScript in your browser. The application does not transmit those field values to the publisher or save them in a database, cookies, local storage, or session storage. Submit controls become available only after the local calculator script loads; the site also blocks network form submissions. You can use hypothetical values. The tools ask only yes/no questions about SSN status, never for an SSN, name, tax ID, account number, home address, email address, or phone number.</p>
  <h2>Hosting and security data</h2>
  <p>Cloudflare delivers the site and may process end-user data such as IP address, request URL, timestamp, user agent, network and security signals, and diagnostic information. Cloudflare may use infrastructure in multiple locations. Its handling is governed by its services terms and <a href="https://www.cloudflare.com/policies/privacy/">privacy policy</a>.</p>
  <p>The site does not operate a separate application logging service, database, or log-export pipeline. Calculator answers are not combined with hosting requests. Cloudflare’s infrastructure records have service-specific retention and remain subject to its policies and service configuration; the publisher does not set or promise a separate deletion period for records controlled by Cloudflare.</p>
  <h2>Email correspondence</h2>
  <p>If you email the publisher, we receive your email address, the message and attachments you send, and associated email metadata. We use this information to respond, investigate corrections or accessibility issues, process privacy requests, and maintain necessary correspondence. Gmail processes these messages under <a href="https://policies.google.com/privacy">Google’s privacy policy</a>. Emailing us does not subscribe you to marketing.</p>
  <h2>Analytics, cookies, advertising, and sale</h2>
  <p>The application code does not include third-party analytics, advertising pixels, session replay, behavioral advertising, or a newsletter form. It does not intentionally sell personal information or share it for cross-context behavioral advertising. Cloudflare may use necessary security or network technologies independently under its service documentation.</p>
  <h2>How information may be used or disclosed</h2>
  <p>Hosting and security data may be used to deliver the site, maintain availability, detect abuse, diagnose failures, and comply with law. It may be processed by Cloudflare and disclosed when legally required. Links to government or other third-party sites are governed by those sites’ privacy practices.</p>
  <h2>Children’s privacy</h2>
  <p>Children under 13 should not email the publisher or submit personal information. If you believe we received information directly from a child under 13, contact <a href={siteContact.emailHref}>{siteContact.email}</a> so we can investigate and delete it or take other action required by applicable law. See the <a href="https://www.ftc.gov/business-guidance/resources/complying-coppa-frequently-asked-questions">FTC COPPA FAQ</a>.</p>
  <h2>State privacy rights</h2>
  <p>You may email <a href={siteContact.emailHref}>{siteContact.email}</a> to request access to, correction of, or deletion of personal information in the publisher’s possession. Use “Privacy request” in the subject line. We will respond under applicable law, explain any lawful exception, and will not discriminate against you for exercising an applicable privacy right. We may request proportionate information to verify your request; do not send a government ID, SSN, or a child’s information. If applicable law provides a right to appeal our response, you may use the same address with the subject “Privacy appeal.” State-law rights and exemptions depend on your location and the law’s applicability.</p>
  <h2>Retention and security</h2>
  <p>Calculator field values are not retained by the application. Routine email correspondence is kept only as long as reasonably needed to answer the request, resolve the reported issue, and maintain a record of the resolution. Information may be kept longer when needed for an unresolved dispute, security incident, or legal obligation. Hosting and email providers may retain backups or security records under their own policies. No website or email service can guarantee absolute security.</p>
  <h2>Changes and contact</h2>
  <p>We will update the effective date when these practices change and describe material changes on this page. Contact <a href={siteContact.emailHref}>{siteContact.email}</a>. Please do not send a child’s name, birth date, SSN, financial documents, tax information, account numbers, or login credentials.</p>
</ArticleLayout>
